A||||54||crash||I ALMOST DIED!!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||crash||11-13-2001||09:18 AM||||THis was totally unexpected. <BR>I was having some argument with my friends about if fieros are good or not and so forth and I got very irate and looked around. I saw this about 9 ft ramp that led from a lower parking lot (where we were at) to an upper level parking lot. I got in my car and told the guys to shut up and watch. I have no idea why I even thought of doing this.<BR>I picked up to about 38-40 and hit the ramp. The fron wheels went up in the air about a foot and a little but... the rear plunged up into the air ?!?!?!?!?!?! ONce I hit the floor Turned around and went back to where my friends were I fast got out of my car and checked the front bumper (gt) I scratched the whole front!!! A couple more feet and I would of been upside down!<BR>NOw I thinkI am going to get a fiero set up for jumps.  Especially since my friends now love my car and don't stop talking about how I was "20 ft abouve ground" hehe.<BR>Does anyone know why this happend in fieros? My beief is the ear engine weight but then again I could be wrong. Anyone have opinions, theory or shuch?<BR>thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||11-13-2001||09:25 AM||||Watched a lot of Duke's of Hazzard when you were a kid too?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dukeboy.jpg"> <P>Yea, when you hit the ramp you preloaded the rear suspension....  and made it boing!<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000002||thomas_l||11-13-2001||09:25 AM||||You need a longer ramp and full throttle going off - even then you'll probably land nose first. I had to get the upper A-arm hardware welded back to the shock towers twice on my high school ride 67 Mustang if you knowwhutimean  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Dont try this at home kids...||||reg||10
