Z||000011||Pilrulz||11-13-2001||06:01 PM||||why did it do this?  well, as tigger said, when you hit the ramp, you compressed the rear suspension, and because for every action there is an equal and opposite reaction, it rapidly expanded at just the right time so that the rear "jumped" off the ramp.  with a longer ramp, it probably wouldn't have happened.  actually, if you have a wing (and this is a long shot...) it may have created lift instead of downforce.<P>pil||||reg||1
