Z||000045||artherd||11-16-2001||12:37 AM||||I really ought to sue you for decreasing my intelligence just by reading this...<P>Wow, I don't even know where to start.<P>So I won't.  Just remember, when the last thing that goes through your mind is your butt; to Think of it as Evolution in Action.<P>And try not to take anyone else with you.<P>Here's an equation for you\.<P>Dumbass^2 + Car == Death In Firery Mess.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by crash:<BR><B>Well.... yeah dumb perhaps, but still a lot of fun.<BR>The fiero is pretty much beat up. <BR>I am getting in touch with a good friend of mine in the grand rapids area to build up a 3.8 "suppy" then no more stunts.<BR>Although I have always had my mind in rallying. There are a couple dirt roads in lowell that I am really tempted to hit.<BR>Was it dimb to do? Maybe. Would I do it again? once I get the upper dog mount replaced... yes.<BR>But I would do my homework and get the physics going before I did it again. And I will videotape it and take pictures.<BR>A car is a car, If you treat it as a person or a living thing you have serious psychological problems. Don't get me wrong, I love my fiero and there is no other car I would prefer to drive (except an Opel Tirga ss).<BR>But It is supposed to be fun!! <BR>My philosofy is "If the car can take it do it"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000046||Mach10||11-16-2001||12:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by crash:<BR><B> <P>And yes, I work in the auto industry so I know fieros are very sturdy cars <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR>UHHH?!?!??? Those A-arms are known to bend under NORMAL driving... Fun yes... Roddable, yes... Sturdy???!?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> Not in it's present state... The space frame is sturdy, the suspension isn't. ESPECIALLY on the front. Try picking up 3 wheels from one corner. That's how "sturdy" the Fiero frame is...<P>Check your alignment. Try that jump again, and check your alignment. Repeat. <BR>A free lowering job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><BR>||||reg||11
Z||000047||crash||11-16-2001||09:42 AM||||well.. I see that there are some people here that are quite offended by my actions and I should apologize to them. <BR>But It also seems to these members that I am quite immature for doing such a fiend.<BR>Well, stupid, yes, perhaps. But not immature. Immature would of been the typical kid in his fiero in the red light revving up his engine and darting out at green without really knowing what lies ahead of him. Or the fiero people that take their cars up to 100+ mph on highways. I think these people are really risking their lives AND the lives of the ones around them. If you have the speed bug, do it right and go to a drag strip or road course. <BR>A lot of drivers out there have less than two years driving experience driving high output machines which the driver is not ready for. <BR>Inmmaturiy is shown daily through excess speeds and wreckless driving (which for some reason in this forum people congratulate you for breaking the law and endagering your life and the lives of others), not by a stupd stunt I did in a deserted parking lot in my car by myself. <BR>So if you are going to get on my case you better stop being hypocrites and get on everybody's case.<BR>peace||||reg||1
